{"timestamp":"2026-05-30T03:25:26.243Z","level":"info","source":"model","message":"response","data":{"model":"qwen36-35b","text":"\n\nI've loaded the **VoidRift Blueprint** (`blueprint.md`). Here's a summary of what it contains:\n\n---\n\n## VoidRift: Decoupled Subsystem Architecture\n\n### What is VoidRift?\nA **highly decoupled, model-agnostic monorepo AI engineering harness** that combines:\n- Multi-agent orchestrator\n- Local-first interactive Terminal User Interface (TUI) built in React and Ink\n- Sovereign, local-first philosophy (no rate limits, no cloud lock-in)\n\n### Core Challenges Solved\n1. **Prompt Cache Starvation** — AI models expensive if re-reading entire codebases every turn\n2. **Write Collisions & Git Corruption** — Concurrent subagents overwriting each other\n3. **Single-Threaded Event Loop Choking** — Heavy processes freezing Node.js runtime\n\n### Five Architectural Pillars\n1. **Pure Composition Root & Event Bus** — Decoupled subsystems communicate via async events\n2. **Three-Partition Context Partitioning** — Governance / Workspace / Work (up to 90% prompt cache reuse)\n3. **Path-Mutex Concurrency Scheduler*","toolCalls":[],"usage":{"promptTokens":5858,"completionTokens":683,"totalTokens":6541}}}
